## 3. Memory Locations

Okay so memory isn't just one giant blob of storage — that would be chaos. Instead:

- Memory is divided into **individual storage compartments** called **memory locations** (or cells).
- Each location can hold a fixed amount of data (usually one "word" — we'll get to that).
- Each location has its own **unique address** so the CPU knows exactly WHERE to go to read/write.
- Think of memory like a giant apartment building 🏢 — each apartment (location) has its own door number (address), and holds its own stuff (data) independently of the other apartments.

```mermaid
